<h1>SecureU — Local Web View Setup & Execution Guide</h1>
<p><strong>Course:</strong> Java Programming / DBMS Lab &bull; <strong>Local Address:</strong> <code>http://localhost:3000</code></p>

<h2>Method 1: 1-Click Web Launcher (Recommended)</h2>
<p>In your project folder, double-click: <strong><code>start-browser-app.bat</code></strong>.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Automatically frees port 3000 from old processes.</li>
  <li>Starts the lightweight local server (<code>local-server.js</code>).</li>
  <li>Automatically launches your default browser at <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Method 2: Via the Java Application (Dual Mode)</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Launch the Java application using <strong><code>Launch-CollegeComplaint.bat</code></strong> or <strong><code>Launch-Terminal-Console.bat</code></strong>.</li>
  <li>Open any browser and navigate to: <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</li>
  <li>Java's built-in HTTP server serves the web portal directly, connected to MySQL JDBC with real-time terminal query logging!</li>
</ol>

<h2>Method 3: From PowerShell or Command Prompt</h2>
<pre>
cd "C:\Users\Hariprasad\Videos\JAVA PROJECT"
node local-server.js
</pre>

<h2>Testing Responsive Mobile View Locally</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open <code>http://localhost:3000</code> in Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge.</li>
  <li>Press <strong>F12</strong> to open Developer Tools.</li>
  <li>Press <strong>Ctrl + Shift + M</strong> to toggle the Device Toolbar.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>iPhone 14 Pro</strong> or <strong>iPad Air</strong> to view the mobile-optimized layout.</li>
</ol>

</body>
</html>
